{
  "id": "COMPOUND:6372 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "Acifluorfen is implicated in the activation of the CX-1 pathway through a series of interconnected molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Acifluorfen acts as a target for Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including (Salicylato-O1,O2)silver and Cyclizidine. These targets are all linked to CX-1, indicating a potential pathway where Acifluorfen may influence CX-1 through the activation of these intermediate molecules. The shared involvement of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial as a common target suggests a possible mechanism where Acifluorfen may modulate cellular processes through this protein, ultimately affecting CX-1. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with Acifluorfen potentially playing a role in the regulation of CX-1 via a network of targets that are themselves involved in cellular signaling or metabolic processes.",
